steps.body:
If the two lines are **parallel**:
- corresponding angles are equal (axiom);
- alternate interior angles are equal;
- co-interior angles are supplementary (add to 180°).
Converses also hold: if any one of these is true, the lines are parallel. **Lines parallel to the same line are parallel to each other.**

Electrons in the outermost shell are **valence electrons**. Atoms with a full outer shell (octet; duplet for He) are inert. Valency = number of electrons gained, lost or shared to complete the octet:
- if valence electrons ≤ 4: valency = valence electrons (Na 1, Mg 2, Al 3, C 4);
- if > 4: valency = 8 − valence electrons (N 3, O 2, Cl 1). Noble gases: 0.
